{
 "slug": "iso-9001-management-review-that-leadership-finds-useful",
 "title": "Management Review That Leadership Finds Useful",
 "desc": "How to turn the ISO 9001 management review from an annual formality into a decision meeting: required inputs and outputs, a one-page agenda and common pitfalls.",
 "cats": [
  "iso"
 ],
 "tags": [
  "management review",
  "ISO 9001",
  "leadership",
  "quality objectives",
  "continual improvement"
 ],
 "body": "<p>Ask a leadership team what they think of the ISO 9001 management review and the usual answer is a polite grimace. Once a year the quality manager presents forty slides, everyone agrees the system is \"suitable, adequate and effective\", the minutes are filed for the auditor, and nothing changes.</p>\n<p>That is a wasted opportunity. The review is the one point at which the standard requires top management to look at how the organization is performing and to decide what to do about it. Run as a decision meeting, it is among the most useful hours leaders spend.</p>\n<h2>What the standard requires</h2>\n<p>Clause 9.3 requires top management to review the quality management system at planned intervals, to ensure that it remains suitable, adequate, effective and aligned with the organization's strategic direction. The clause lists what the review must consider and what it must produce. Certification bodies report that this clause changed very little in the 2026 edition.</p>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Required inputs</th><th>Question it answers for leaders</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Status of actions from previous reviews</td><td>Did we do what we decided?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Changes in external and internal issues</td><td>What has changed around us and inside the business?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Customer satisfaction and feedback from interested parties</td><td>What do customers and others think of us?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Extent to which quality objectives have been met</td><td>Are we hitting our targets?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Process performance and conformity of products and services</td><td>Are our processes delivering?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Nonconformities and corrective actions</td><td>What went wrong, and has it stopped?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Monitoring and measurement results</td><td>What do the numbers show?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Audit results</td><td>What did internal and external audits find?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Performance of external providers</td><td>Are our suppliers reliable?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Adequacy of resources</td><td>Do we have the people, equipment and budget we need?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Effectiveness of actions on risks and opportunities</td><td>Did our precautions and initiatives work?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Opportunities for improvement</td><td>What should we do next?</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>The required outputs are decisions and actions on three things: opportunities for improvement, any need for changes to the quality management system, and resource needs. You must keep a record of the results.</p>\n<h2>Why most reviews fail</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>They report and do not decide.</strong> Data is presented and noted. No one is asked to choose anything.</li>\n<li><strong>They happen once a year.</strong> By then the data is stale and the list is too long to discuss properly.</li>\n<li><strong>They belong to the quality manager.</strong> Leaders attend as an audience and not as owners.</li>\n<li><strong>They are separate from running the business.</strong> The same people discuss the same performance in a different meeting the following week.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Turn it into a decision meeting</h2>\n<figure style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Diagram. Five input boxes on the left: actions from last review; changes in context, customers and regulations; performance of objectives, processes, customers and suppliers; audits and nonconformities; and resources, risks and opportunities. Arrows lead to a central box, the review meeting of 60 to 90 minutes with data sent in advance and decisions recorded in the room. Three output boxes on the right: improvement actions with owner and date; changes to the quality system; and resources approved or reallocated.\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" viewBox=\"0 0 502.56 249.912\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\">\n <metadata>\n  <rdf:RDF xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:cc=\"http://creativecommons.org/ns#\" xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\">\n   <cc:Work>\n    <dc:type rdf:resource=\"http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/StillImage\"/>\n    <dc:date>2026-11-10T01:57:28.388206</dc:date>\n    <dc:format>image/svg+xml</dc:format>\n    <dc:creator>\n     <cc:Agent>\n      <dc:title>Matplotlib v3.11.2, https://matplotlib.org/</dc:title>\n     </cc:Agent>\n    </dc:creator>\n   </cc:Work>\n  </rdf:RDF>\n </metadata>\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 249.912 \nL 502.56 249.912 \nL 502.56 0 \nL 0 0 \nL 0 249.912 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 14.3532 58.80222 \nL 134.658 58.80222 \nQ 139.5684 58.80222 139.5684 56.4183 \nL 139.5684 26.6193 \nQ 139.5684 24.23538 134.658 24.23538 \nL 14.3532 24.23538 \nQ 9.4428 24.23538 9.4428 26.6193 \nL 9.4428 56.4183 \nQ 9.4428 58.80222 14.3532 58.80222 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #cfe6f3; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 141.28704 41.5188 \nQ 165.348 72.50976 188.654755 102.52929 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 187.956153 99.020451 \nL 188.654755 102.52929 \nL 185.428522 100.982869 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #0b6fa4; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_4\">\n    <path d=\"M 14.3532 100.52082 \nL 134.658 100.52082 \nQ 139.5684 100.52082 139.5684 98.1369 \nL 139.5684 68.3379 \nQ 139.5684 65.95398 134.658 65.95398 \nL 14.3532 65.95398 \nQ 9.4428 65.95398 9.4428 68.3379 \nL 9.4428 98.1369 \nQ 9.4428 100.52082 14.3532 100.52082 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #cfe6f3; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_5\">\n    <path d=\"M 141.28704 83.2374 \nQ 165.348 98.73288 188.374989 113.562473 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 186.550938 110.484676 \nL 188.374989 113.562473 \nL 184.818321 113.175037 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #0b6fa4; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_6\">\n    <path d=\"M 14.3532 142.23942 \nL 134.658 142.23942 \nQ 139.5684 142.23942 139.5684 139.8555 \nL 139.5684 110.0565 \nQ 139.5684 107.67258 134.658 107.67258 \nL 14.3532 107.67258 \nQ 9.4428 107.67258 9.4428 110.0565 \nL 9.4428 139.8555 \nQ 9.4428 142.23942 14.3532 142.23942 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #cfe6f3; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_7\">\n    <path d=\"M 141.28704 124.956 \nQ 165.348 124.956 188.179123 124.956 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 184.979123 123.356 \nL 188.179123 124.956 \nL 184.979123 126.556 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #0b6fa4; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_8\">\n    <path d=\"M 14.3532 183.95802 \nL 134.658 183.95802 \nQ 139.5684 183.95802 139.5684 181.5741 \nL 139.5684 151.7751 \nQ 139.5684 149.39118 134.658 149.39118 \nL 14.3532 149.39118 \nQ 9.4428 149.39118 9.4428 151.7751 \nL 9.4428 181.5741 \nQ 9.4428 183.95802 14.3532 183.95802 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #cfe6f3; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_9\">\n    <path d=\"M 141.28704 166.6746 \nQ 165.348 151.17912 188.374989 136.349527 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 184.818321 136.736963 \nL 188.374989 136.349527 \nL 186.550938 139.427324 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #0b6fa4; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_10\">\n    <path d=\"M 14.3532 225.67662 \nL 134.658 225.67662 \nQ 139.5684 225.67662 139.5684 223.2927 \nL 139.5684 193.4937 \nQ 139.5684 191.10978 134.658 191.10978 \nL 14.3532 191.10978 \nQ 9.4428 191.10978 9.4428 193.4937 \nL 9.4428 223.2927 \nQ 9.4428 225.67662 14.3532 225.67662 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #cfe6f3; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_11\">\n    <path d=\"M 141.28704 208.3932 \nQ 165.348 177.40224 188.654755 147.38271 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 185.428522 148.929131 \nL 188.654755 147.38271 \nL 187.956153 150.891549 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #0b6fa4; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_12\">\n    <path d=\"M 196.038 182.76606 \nL 306.522 182.76606 \nQ 311.4324 182.76606 311.4324 180.38214 \nL 311.4324 69.52986 \nQ 311.4324 67.14594 306.522 67.14594 \nL 196.038 67.14594 \nQ 191.1276 67.14594 191.1276 69.52986 \nL 191.1276 180.38214 \nQ 191.1276 182.76606 196.038 182.76606 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #fbe6d8; stroke: #e07a3a; stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_13\">\n    <path d=\"M 367.902 77.87358 \nL 488.2068 77.87358 \nQ 493.1172 77.87358 493.1172 75.48966 \nL 493.1172 38.5389 \nQ 493.1172 36.15498 488.2068 36.15498 \nL 367.902 36.15498 \nQ 362.9916 36.15498 362.9916 38.5389 \nL 362.9916 75.48966 \nQ 362.9916 77.87358 367.902 77.87358 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #e4f1d3; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_14\">\n    <path d=\"M 313.15104 110.65248 \nQ 337.212 83.83338 360.302357 58.096144 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.3; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 356.558474 59.573756 \nL 360.302357 58.096144 \nL 359.238117 61.977818 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #4d7f12; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.3; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_15\">\n    <path d=\"M 367.902 135.08766 \nL 488.2068 135.08766 \nQ 493.1172 135.08766 493.1172 132.70374 \nL 493.1172 95.75298 \nQ 493.1172 93.36906 488.2068 93.36906 \nL 367.902 93.36906 \nQ 362.9916 93.36906 362.9916 95.75298 \nL 362.9916 132.70374 \nQ 362.9916 135.08766 367.902 135.08766 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #e4f1d3; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_16\">\n    <path d=\"M 313.15104 124.956 \nQ 337.212 119.59218 359.854338 114.544608 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.3; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 355.948936 113.571041 \nL 359.854338 114.544608 \nL 356.732243 117.084789 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #4d7f12; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.3; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_17\">\n    <path d=\"M 367.902 192.30174 \nL 488.2068 192.30174 \nQ 493.1172 192.30174 493.1172 189.91782 \nL 493.1172 152.96706 \nQ 493.1172 150.58314 488.2068 150.58314 \nL 367.902 150.58314 \nQ 362.9916 150.58314 362.9916 152.96706 \nL 362.9916 189.91782 \nQ 362.9916 192.30174 367.902 192.30174 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #e4f1d3; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_18\">\n    <path d=\"M 313.15104 139.25952 \nQ 337.212 155.35098 360.0648 170.634448 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.3; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 358.072987 167.136924 \nL 360.0648 170.634448 \nL 356.071693 170.129385 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pf53f51ee7b)\" style=\"fill: #4d7f12; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.3; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_1\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(50.060686 38.430873)\">Actions from</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(54.049936 50.636165)\">last review</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_2\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(36.378647 79.281254)\">Changes in context,</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(30.851663 91.532108)\">customers, regulations</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_3\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(48.538139 115.738849)\">Performance:</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(31.65217 127.172742)\">objectives, processes,</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(34.591584 139.423597)\">customers, suppliers</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_4\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(54.146123 163.54111)\">Audits and</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(43.42628 175.837527)\">nonconformities</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_5\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(42.994069 204.600952)\">Resources, risks</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.1px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(40.916545 216.735369)\">and opportunities</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_6\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.8px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(218.383813 94.038824)\">Review meeting</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.8px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(251.28 104.991645)\"/>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.8px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(220.42775 121.55584)\">60–90 minutes</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.8px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(208.091938 134.861285)\">data sent in advance</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.8px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(211.418063 148.17498)\">decisions recorded</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.8px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(227.819063 161.484551)\">in the room</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_7\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(386.965509 53.009084)\">Improvement actions</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(388.16447 66.356765)\">with owner and date</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_8\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(398.260642 110.116172)\">Changes to the</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(399.694986 122.760298)\">quality system</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_9\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(387.725478 167.338033)\">Resources approved</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(401.033361 180.685714)\">or reallocated</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_10\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9.8px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b6fa4\" x=\"74.5056\" y=\"15.29568\" transform=\"rotate(-0 74.5056 15.29568)\">Inputs</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_11\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9.8px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #e07a3a\" x=\"251.28\" y=\"53.4384\" transform=\"rotate(-0 251.28 53.4384)\">Decide</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_12\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9.8px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #4d7f12\" x=\"428.0544\" y=\"24.83136\" transform=\"rotate(-0 428.0544 24.83136)\">Outputs</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_13\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.6px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(185.363016 211.12881)\">If no decision changes anything,</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.6px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(188.011547 224.66222)\">the review has not done its job.</text>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"pf53f51ee7b\">\n   <rect x=\"5.76\" y=\"5.76\" width=\"491.04\" height=\"238.392\"/>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>The review takes five groups of inputs and must produce three kinds of output. The meeting itself is for deciding.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Send the data beforehand.</strong> A one- or two-page pack with trends, issued a week ahead, lets the meeting start from questions. Show each measure as a trend against its target, and mark the items that need a decision.</p>\n<p><strong>Have process owners present their own results.</strong> The sales manager speaks to customer feedback, the production manager to process performance, the purchasing manager to suppliers. The quality manager coordinates and presents audit results.</p>\n<p><strong>Frame each item as a decision.</strong> \"On-time delivery fell from 94% to 88% in the quarter; the main cause is late material from two suppliers. Options: dual-source, or hold more stock. Recommendation: dual-source.\" Leaders then choose.</p>\n<p><strong>Record decisions in the room.</strong> Each action gets an owner and a date before the meeting ends. That record is the evidence the standard asks for.</p>\n<p><strong>Review more often.</strong> \"Planned intervals\" does not mean annually. A quarterly review of 60 to 90 minutes works better than an annual half-day. You can also cover the inputs across your existing monthly management meetings, provided every input is addressed over the year and you keep records.</p>\n<h2>A one-page agenda</h2>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Time</th><th>Item</th><th>Lead</th><th>Decision sought</th></tr>\n<tr><td>10 min</td><td>Actions from last review</td><td>Chair</td><td>Close, extend or escalate each open action</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10 min</td><td>What has changed: customers, market, regulations, people, systems</td><td>General manager</td><td>Any change to scope, policy or objectives?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>15 min</td><td>Customers: satisfaction, complaints, returns</td><td>Sales</td><td>Top one or two issues to act on</td></tr>\n<tr><td>20 min</td><td>Performance: objectives, process measures, product conformity, suppliers</td><td>Process owners</td><td>Action on any measure off target</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10 min</td><td>Audits, nonconformities and corrective actions</td><td>Quality</td><td>Recurring problems that need resources</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10 min</td><td>Risks and opportunities: what happened, what is new</td><td>All</td><td>Update the register; approve new actions</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10 min</td><td>Resources and improvement priorities</td><td>General manager</td><td>Approve people, equipment, training or budget</td></tr>\n<tr><td>5 min</td><td>Summary of decisions</td><td>Chair</td><td>Confirm owners and dates</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>The agenda covers every required input in 90 minutes. If you are moving to the 2026 edition, add an item on transition progress; see the <a href=\"post/iso-9001-2026-transition-plan.html\">transition plan</a>. Quality culture and ethical behaviour, which the new edition makes a responsibility of top management, also belong on this agenda once or twice a year.</p>\n<h2>What good minutes look like</h2>\n<p>Keep them to one page: date and attendees, the data pack attached, and a table of decisions with owner and date. An auditor will look for three things: that the required inputs were considered, that decisions were made, and that actions from the previous review were followed up. A long narrative adds nothing.</p>\n<h2>Signs the review is working</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Leaders ask for the data pack when it is late.</li>\n<li>Each review produces a small number of decisions that would not otherwise have been made.</li>\n<li>Actions are closed by the next review.</li>\n<li>Resource requests are argued from data and are sometimes approved.</li>\n<li>The findings of <a href=\"post/iso-9001-internal-audits-that-find-real-problems.html\">internal audits</a> and the <a href=\"post/iso-9001-risk-based-thinking-in-practice.html\">risk register</a> change as a result of the discussion.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Want a second pair of eyes?</strong> Chmltech helps Canadian organizations build, simplify and audit quality management systems. <a href=\"../book.html\">Book a strategy call</a> or <a href=\"../contact.html\">ask a question</a>.</p>\n<h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.sgs.com/en-gb/showcases/iso-9001-2026-key-updates-and-transition-guidance\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">SGS: ISO 9001:2026 key updates and transition guidance</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.dnv.us/assurance/Management-Systems/new-iso/transition/iso-9001-revision/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">DNV: ISO 9001:2026 standard revision</a></li></ul>\n<h2>More in this series</h2><ul><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-2026-what-changed-from-2015.html\">ISO 9001:2026: what changed from 2015</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-2026-transition-plan.html\">Your ISO 9001:2026 transition plan</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-for-small-and-mid-sized-businesses.html\">ISO 9001 for small and mid-sized businesses</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-internal-audits-that-find-real-problems.html\">Internal audits that find real problems</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-risk-based-thinking-in-practice.html\">Risk-based thinking in practice</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-and-ai-using-ai-tools-inside-a-quality-system.html\">ISO 9001 and AI</a></li><li><a href=\"post/integrated-management-system-iso-9001-14001-45001.html\">Integrating ISO 9001, ISO 14001 and ISO 45001</a></li></ul>",
